  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I would like there to be some way to get whether someone's avatar is being culled through Udon. I would imagine this looks something like \"bool playerApi.GetAvatarIsCulled()\". Which would return tru if that player is being culled (due to avatar culling limit, or avatar culling distance, i.e. the player appears as the semi-transparent diamonds \"avatar\")\n\nThis could help me with some interactions between avatar visuals and my game worlds. For example, in Murder and freeze tag, I could apply additional indicators to culled players to help with visual clarity, especially through the spectator screen. I could also use this to make my portrait cameras work better in some other games which take snapshots of player's heads onto rendertextures.",
